From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:44:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): a restart with no turn running carries
 background subagents and their helpers to their boundaries

The per-turn carry (gateway.restart_turn_handoff_per_turn) ran the background subagents on to their step boundaries only when a chat turn was running. With none (a chat that started a background subagent and ended its turn), the restart wait returned at once, since the subagents are not work it waits for (gateway.restart_wait_delegations is off), so the carry never started. The stop then handed the subagents over the 0016 way with restart_handoff_grace_seconds: a running foreground terminal command was moved to the background (yielded_to_background), the subagent started its next model call, the stop cut it, and the next gateway's subagent ran the command again. The restart wait now starts the carry when background subagents run that delegation.restart_handoff hands over: the profile goes to the next gateway at once, and each subagent finishes its command and its tool round on the old gateway and stops before its next model call; the next gateway resumes it with the real tool result in its transcript.

A carried subagent also stopped its own subagents (its helpers) with it, cutting a helper's model call. Each helper in a turn is now carried the same way: it runs on to its own next step boundary, the subagent's stop waits for it (up to the same limit), its unit goes to the next gateway as unfinished with the state it had there, and it does not wake the subagent here. A helper not in a turn, or with no resume record, stops with the subagent as before.
